# DASM - Disassemble a Z80 binary

```text
B0:DASM
```

## Read and list

At DASM's prompt, R reads a file and H lists commands. N sets the
logical length in hex, excluding CP/M record padding. For a program
known to contain five bytes at 0100H:

```text
RPROGRAM.COM
N5
P100,105
```

## Write source

```text
SREBUILD.ASM
P100,105
QL100,105
Z
G
```

S names the staged output. P emits the prologue and equates. QL lists
into the output, Z finishes it and G leaves DASM. Use the actual address
bounds of your input. A .DSY produced by [DSYM](DSYM.HLP) supplies
symbol names.
